Upstream bug: https://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-147602 (fixed in 6.11.2)
Backport of qtbase 08e464f85597 (6.11 pick of dev a481ede673e8).
Subject: [PATCH] Fix regression in QImage::toCGImage() with custom color space

qt_mac_cgImageFormatForImage() returned a vImage_CGImageFormat holding a raw
CGColorSpaceRef whose owning QCFType local was released on return, so
QImage::toCGImage() passed a freed colour space to CGImageCreate. The named
sRGB space is cached by CoreGraphics and survives; one created from the
image's ICC profile does not. Crashes (EXC_BREAKPOINT in CFGetTypeID) for any
QImage with a valid QColorSpace, e.g. QCursor from a PNG with gAMA/sRGB/iCCP
chunks via QCocoaCursor::createCursorFromPixmap -> imageFromQImage.

Fix: return a Qt-owned QCGImageFormat that keeps the colour space alive in a
QCFType. Drop this patch when moving to Qt >= 6.11.2.

